cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "quantum_al: correlation-aware active learning for materials discovery"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Kapoor"
    given-names: "Arnav"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-9818-7908"
    affiliation: "Indian Institute of Science Education and Research Bhopal"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arnavk23/quantum_al"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - active learning
  - materials discovery
  - Bayesian experimental design
  - expected information gain
  - uncertainty quantification
  - quantum-inspired algorithms
abstract: >-
  A Python package for building and rigorously benchmarking multi-property
  acquisition criteria for active learning in materials discovery:
  information-theoretic criteria from Bayesian optimal experimental design
  (joint and correlation-blind expected information gain, total correlation,
  greedy batch EIG), diagnostics that explain when such criteria can differ,
  a synthetic testbed with tunable cross-property correlation, a real-data
  Materials Project benchmark harness with nine classical baselines and
  corrected paired statistics, and a quantum-inspired covariance formalism
  with a verified Qiskit circuit realization.
